course: dictionary
lesson: 2066
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one the author means. Console can be a verb (said con-SOLE) or a noun (said CON-sole). Read the words around it to find the clues.
explain: To console someone means to comfort them when they are sad or upset. Ollie felt «ashamed and scared», so a friend who consoled him would listen and say something kind. Try your meaning in the sentence: does it still make sense?
explain: A console can also be a games machine: «Dad takes the console away for a whole week.» It can also be a panel of buttons, switches and screens, like the one a pilot uses. Phrases such as «games console» and «control console» help you pick the right meaning.
fact: Console (verb, said con-SOLE) means to comfort someone who is sad or upset and help them feel better.
fact: Console (noun, said CON-sole) means a games machine you connect to a TV or hold in your hands, or a panel with buttons and switches for controlling a machine.
fact: «Most consoles have parental controls that can block games above a chosen age rating.»
fact: Useful phrases: «console someone», «games console», «control console».
fact: A pilot or a spaceship captain sits at the console to control the plane or the ship.
exercise: «Dad takes the console away for a whole week.» What is the console here? | A quiet room for reading | *A games machine you play video games on | A kind word for someone who is sad | A soft chair for the sofa
exercise: Ella's friend is crying after losing a match. What does it mean to console her? | *Listen to her and say something kind to help her feel better | Take her game away from her | Shout at her to stop crying | Walk off and say nothing at all
exercise: «The captain sat at the console and checked every switch.» What is the console? | *A panel of buttons, switches and screens | A type of spaceship | To comfort someone who is sad | A games machine for playing at home
test: «Most consoles have parental controls that can block games above a chosen age rating.» Which meaning of console fits? | A type of lamp | A quiet room for reading | To comfort someone who is sad | *A games machine
test: Mia's brother is upset after losing. Her mum says, «Go and console him.» What does console mean? | To tell him off loudly | *To comfort him and help him feel better | To play a game with him against his will | To switch him off
exam: «The pilot checked every button on the console before take-off.» Which meaning of console is right? | To comfort someone who is sad | A kind hug for a friend | A games machine you connect to a TV | *A panel with buttons, switches and screens for controlling a plane
